{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this","id":1214387,"title":"Since I don't know where to put this","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-02T18:42:47-07:00","id":1214387,"title":"Since I don't know where to put this","content":"What are the primary differences of old and chronicles of darkness? Also, what are the pros and cons of apocalypse and forsaken, primarily because I know apocalypse was very popular","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T18:58:09-07:00","id":1214390,"title":"","content":"Pretty much different in every way.<br /> <br /> Different setting, different game mechanics, and different themes. While both are about supernatural monsters that have lived among humanity from the beginning, World of Darkness is about how the world is coming to an end and with massive stakes, while Chronicles of Darkness leans more and the supernaturals' day to day life among humanity and with their respective supernatural societies with (relatively) much smaller and personal stakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T19:51:56-07:00","id":1214404,"title":"","content":"Some sister games share relatively similar premises. Most notably, Vampire: The Masquerade and Vampire: The Requiem are both recognizably about similar visions of vampires clinging to their humanity, forming dynasties of blood, and squabbling for power over one another as they manipulate the living to ease their unlives and achieve their goals.<br /> <br /> Things diverge from there. Werewolf: The Apocalypse and Werewolf: The Forsaken are both about people who awaken to a half-spirit heritage and become hardy, shapechanging world-walkers who wage battles across both the body and soul of the world. But Apocalypse's war, its enemy, and its counterorganization are all global in nature, while the Forsaken often face more personal threats and are more likely to splinter in local interests. The spirit world of Apocalypse faces a deadly evil taint which cannot ultimately be reasoned or compromised with, threatening the natural balance, whereas Forsaken's spirit world is muddier, red in tooth and claw, mostly cautious and opportunistic if you get too careless, but without such a cosmic threat to taint it.<br /> <br /> Some other gamelines diverge wildly in basic premise. Demon: The Fallen and Demon: The Descent, while they share certain influences, are wildly different games about fundamentally different conflicts.<br /> <br /> One contrast that can be drawn between the two gamelines is in the titular darkness. As a general trend, the World of Darkness leans towards an inner heart of darkness, a sort of corruption of the soul. The World of Darkness is an impressionist world where violent crime rates are higher and horrifically cynical businesses, like snuff film companies, operate concealed within society. The Chronicles of Darkness tend more towards darkness as mystery and the fear of the unknown. Both settings have their share of pessimism about human behavior, but where the World of Darkness deliberately exaggerates to make its point, the Chronicles lean more towards portraying down-to-earth humans in a dangerous and isolating world. Ordinary life goes on in the World of Darkness because the monsters have the power, and they exercise it to erase their presence from human knowledge. Ordinary life goes on in the Chronicles of Darkness because even the local monsters often don't know what's lurking in the fog on the outskirts of town, but everyone shares the instinctive sense that whatever it is, they're probably safer and better off leaving it alone and pretending it's not there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T03:38:18-07:00","id":1214512,"title":"","content":"World of darkness feels much more nihilistic to me. The end is nigh, and you cannot change it. Everything you do will be washed away, and nothing you do matters in the long run.<br /> <br /> Chronicles is much more of a personal element of horror. You are a monster, you will be monstrous at some point, maybe even have no choice but to be a monster, but you still have choices, make decisions, and what you do might matter in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:24:10-07:00","id":1214523,"title":"","content":"One big difference between WoD and CoD is that in CoD most people have had somekind of supernatural experience, no matter how minor, but the vast majority chose to go into denial, they don't want to know, which might seem dangerous, but in practice is safer, were as in WoD I believe most people are completely unaware of the Supernatural.<br /> <br /> Also WoD mostly draws from Judeo-Christian Mythology aa far as know with a few exceptions, but CoD has many Gods, from the Godmachine, True Fae, Incarnae, Superneral Creatures, Chthonic Gods, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:35:20-07:00","id":1214594,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys! For the future where would y'all ssayni should put posts like this in<br /> <br /> So basically it's about scope and tone, world is the end, you are just another cog, while chronicle is a personal, solitary experience. Though, each have their horror elements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T08:03:03-07:00","id":1214604,"title":"","content":"Building on Stupid Loserman's analysis on Apocalypse and Forsaken specifically: the Garou are warriors, while the Uratha are hunters. Their cultures, psychologies, worldviews, and supernatural abilities follow suit. Oh, and the natural and spirit worlds, along with their denizens, are presented more idealistically in Apocalypse. In Forsaken, well, things are much less so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T08:05:45-07:00","id":1214606,"title":"","content":"WoD is frequently more external horror - something is going to kill/maim/eat me.<br /> CofD is frequently more internal horror - what have I become?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T08:31:53-07:00","id":1214619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214594#post1214594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks guys! For the future where would y'all ssayni should put posts like this in</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a perfectly good place for it. If you have questions about a specific game line you could ask in that game\u2019s subforum. Most lines also have a \u201cask a simple question, get a simple answer\u201d thread as well, which are a good resource.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214594#post1214594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically it's about scope and tone, world is the end, you are just another cog, while chronicle is a personal, solitary experience. Though, each have their horror elements</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s one of the key tonal differences, yes. Although I wouldn\u2019t necessarily describe Chronicles as solitary - most of the game lines have a focus on group play. It\u2019s just that CofD focuses on more intimate stories of those characters\u2019 interpersonal experiences, where WoD focuses on grand scale stories concerning the fate of the world.<br /> <br /> Looking at the werewolf games as examples, since you were interested in those, in<br /> Apocalypse you play the soldiers in a losing war to save the planet from physical and spiritual devistation at the hands of corrupt humans and spirits tainted by disharmony. There is a heavy focus on rage, and the game plays up the futility of your struggle, while simultaneously emphasizing its importance. You\u2019ve lost the war, the world is ending, but at least you can use these last waning days to fuck up the ones responsible as much as they\u2019ve fucked the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> In Forsaken, you play memers of the keystone species in the spritual ecosystem. As descendents of the ultimate predator, you are driven to hunt, and in hunting, to maintain the delicate balance between spirit and flesh, within your territory and within yourself. There is no grand conflict or great enemy to war against, though there are many threats to you, your pack, and your territory. Rage is still present, apropos of werewolves, but rather than righteous indignation at the world\u2019s sealed fate, the rage is a consequence of disharmony. Deny your predatory nature and it seeths under the surface until the moon, or the taste of blood, or some other trigger sets it free and the rage takes control. Embrace your nature to the exclusion of your humanity and you may have control, but you become unable to lead a normal life, as you lose the ability to resist becoming the wolf at the slightest of urges.<br /> <br /> So both game lines play with similar themes - harmony between the material and the spiritual, the balance of nature and natural ecosystems, the werewolf as a metaphor for uncontrolled anger, etc. But Apocalypse handles it through a global and fatalistic lens, where Forsaken handles it through a more personal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-03-2018, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:00:28-07:00","id":1214682,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok<br /> <br /> In terms of theme, what is the difference of the two? I only understand apocalypse is about controlling what you are, not giving into bestial temptation, but forsaken seems to be also focused on that, so I'm confused. Also are the forsaken werewolf forms more powerful than apocalypse ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:32:59-07:00","id":1214693,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: W:tA vs. W:tF</b><br /> <br /> While I can't speak to how other St's approach the game, for me, the central Them of W:tA was &quot;Rage against the Dying of the Light&quot;. The battle of the Apocalypse was truthfully over except for tiny glimmers of hope. The Garou Nation was determined that no matter how bleak the situation became, they would fight to the bitter end. It generally framed the Garou as <i>Warriors</i> - the mightiest of the mighty..and yet that might was rarely enough, and often caused more problems then it solved. The gameline had a deeply fatalistic thread that was spot on appropriate for the World of Darkness at the time.<br /> <br /> For W:tF , the Theme is &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;. The Uratha are the descendants of a predator god , and predation is a central conceit of the setting. No matter what situation a Uratha finds themselves in , they view just about every interaction as Predator or Prey. The setting also plays up the themes of Pack - the family you choose - against all the forces arrayed against you.<br /> The Uratha are framed as the supreme <i>Hunters</i> - they aren't fighting a war as much are trying to reconcile that predators nature with the world around them.<br /> <br /> There are of course conceptual overlaps, but at their hearts they use the imagery of Werewolves to tell very different stories.<br /> <br /> As far as their prowess is concerned, its almost apple and oranges. Each is relatively powerful compared to the rest of their respective gamelines, but the Uratha are less overwhelmingly potent than the Garou (at least in terms of sheer physicality).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T11:55:05-07:00","id":1214705,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about W:TF, but another good way to look at W:TA is the Norse mythology. In particular Ragnar\u00f6k. There is a very strong parallel between the two:<br /> <br /> - You know you are going to die;<br /> - You know mistakes, crucial ones, were done in the past and they are crippling you;<br /> - You know the world, as you know it, will be destroyed;<br /> - You're not taking it lying, you're taking as many of them with you as you can, and;<br /> - You hope, that you'll be able to save, through your fighting and sacrifice, just enough to allow the world to be reborn into the Paradis it was meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 05-03-2018, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:11:18-07:00","id":1214717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214682#post1214682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh ok<br /> <br /> In terms of theme, what is the difference of the two? I only understand apocalypse is about controlling what you are, not giving into bestial temptation, but forsaken seems to be also focused on that, so I'm confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m only passingly familiar with Apocalypse, so I can\u2019t help you much on that. With Forsaken though, I wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s about not giving into bestial temptation, and a character who did see their lycanthropy that way would be very likely to end up like the werewolves of classic media like <i>The Wolfman</i> - an ordinary human most of the time who uncontrollably transforms into a monster and kills indiscriminately for a few hours whenever he\u2019s faced with a certain stimulus (the full moon, in this particular case). Rather, Forsaken is about owning your bestial nature, without letting it own you. See, in Forsaken there\u2019s a stat called Harmony, which is rated on a 0-10 scale. Doing werewolf-y things like hunting, spending time in the spirit world, spending long periods away from other people, etc., makes that number go down. On the other hand, going too long without hunting or entering the spirit world, or otherwise trying to resist your werewolf nature makes that number go up. At higher Harmony levels, it\u2019s more difficult to shape shift, and the triggers that can set you into a death rage get more pervasive and harder to resist, and when you go into death rage it lasts longer. At lower harmony levels, shapeshifting becomes so easy that sometimes it just happens by accident, and you gain Bans - behaviors that you are supernaturally compelled to follow, just like a spirit. So ideally you want your Harmony to be as close to 5 as possible. The goal is not to deny your predatory urges completely, but to manage them carefully so you strike just the right balance between human being and predator spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Callishka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1213031-investigation-rules-when-to-add-complications?p=1214462#post1214462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also are the forsaken werewolf forms more powerful than apocalypse ones</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s difficult to measure, since the two games use fairly different rules systems. Apocalypse\u2019s forms do tend to give bigger bonuses to physical attributes than Forsaken\u2019s forms do. However, as of 2nd editition, each of Forsaken\u2019s forms has a unique ability according to its role in the hunt. Human form is supernaturally good at blending in. Near-human form is supernaturally intimidating. Wolf form is incredibly fast. Near-wolf form can inflict free debuffs on its victims. Wolf-man form regenerates at a ridiculous rate and can kill lesser enemies in a single roll, but has a time limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-03-2018, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:20:20-07:00","id":1214725,"title":"","content":"So basically, garou represent the might, rage filled force of nature of werewolves. Forsaken on the other hand, represents the bestial, spiritual aspect, like what it means to be of human and bestial nature<br /> <br /> As for power, it seems garou are seen as the more powerful of the two, but uratha, despite being split between pure and forsaken, are much more willing to work in combined packs, allowing adaptation. Though, I'm afraid that's an unfair assumption, since on a wide scale, garou do value being a pack and are not split like uratha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 05-03-2018, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:30:39-07:00","id":1214733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214725#post1214725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically, garou represent the might, rage filled force of nature of werewolves. Forsaken on the other hand, represents the bestial, spiritual aspect, like what it means to be of human and bestial nature</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Forsaken, I would say less bestial and more predatory, but yes, that\u2019s a fairly accurate take on how each game treats the nature of the werewolf. It\u2019s also important to note each game\u2019s history. The Garou are the soldiers of a generations-long war for the fate of the Earth. The Forsaken are the inheritors of a sacred duty to maintain the balance of the spirit world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T12:59:28-07:00","id":1214740,"title":"","content":"I dont know Apocalypse really well but my gut feeling want to say that Apocalypse werewolves are better warriors while Uratha makes for better hunters.<br /> Of course thats the very general baseline, individual characters can differ greatly from that, based on build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:15:02-07:00","id":1214786,"title":"","content":"Final question. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> said, apocalypse is more external horror while forsaken is internal. How do they primarily show these, and specifically, is the rage system in apocalypse used for this aspect too, As it seems to be both an external and internal sort of horror, yet apocalypse seems to be the most combat oriented of any darkness game, so I don't know how much social interaction garou are in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:37:58-07:00","id":1214797,"title":"","content":"Yes. Apocalypse is more combat orientated, but it is also a very social game. Wolves and human are both, usually, very social animals and so do the Garou. They don't live in a void, they interact daily with their pack mate, the Caern member, their Totem, the Spirits, their tribemates, Garou from other tribes (and all 13 tribes don't always have cordial relationship), human around them, kinfolk and &quot;normals&quot;. Media and law enforcement to either hide their fight or take it on the public forum...and much more.<br /> <br /> the W:TA external horror, is both in the actual physical form of the Agent of the Wyrm, the corruption (physical, moral, spiritual and psychologicsl) they are spreading, the 3 lost tribes and lost Fera...usual from their own claws, the unavoidable collateral damage and the sheer horror of the ultimate hopelessness of you action. HELLO Hanaro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 05-03-2018, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:40:04-07:00","id":1214799,"title":"","content":"So if you have not been fighting to keep rage down, you can prove a danger to your friends too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:44:22-07:00","id":1214800,"title":"","content":"To a certain extend yes. How many Lost Cubs have ripped to shreds Loved Ones (friend, parents, siblings girlfriend/boyfriend) during their First Change. Plenty of Kinfolk (human carrier of the Garou gene) gets mistreated or downright harmed by those who should care and protect them.<br /> <br /> Even in human form, a character with high Rage score can go for Calm to Violent AF in 0.000003 seconds flat. Because ultimately, they are monsters, killing machines, and damn good at it too, whose primary role is to protect Gaia at all cost.<br /> <br /> whereas in Forsaken they are Apex Predator that's who hunts their prey and that's A big difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 05-03-2018, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T15:47:12-07:00","id":1214802,"title":"","content":"So they make up the external horror perfectly. And how does forsaken handle the internal horror<br /> <br /> Also this is my last question, once answered I'm gonna call for a mod to shut it down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:24:04-07:00","id":1214891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214797#post1214797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the W:TA external horror, is both in the actual physical form of the Agent of the Wyrm, the corruption (physical, moral, spiritual and psychologicsl) they are spreading, the 3 lost tribes and lost Fera...usual from their own claws, the unavoidable collateral damage and the sheer horror of the ultimate hopelessness of you action. HELLO Hanaro.</div> </div> </div> </div>... which is almost the same dangers in WtF - only they are not connected to one, large meta-story. I dip sometimes as recreating WtA stuff in WtF and it's fairly easy. Just see comparison list of main game antagonists you mentioned...<br /> <br /> <b>WtA Element - WtF Element</b><ul><li>Agents of Wyrm - Bale Hounds and Maeljin cultists ( Bale Hounds wins as they are <i>secret </i>'dark forces worshiping werewolves' )</li> <li>Wyrm Corruption - Wounds, almost literal comparison</li> <li>3 Lost Tribes - Pure Tribes ( see below ) and countless lesser/unknown Firstborn mini-Tribes, all you need</li> <li>Lost Fera - We have countless monsterous Hosts that eat humans from inside and become human-animal hybrids. And various Changing Breeds in <b>War Against the Pure</b> book ( yeah, I know it's weird place to look for them )</li> <li>Rage - Death Rage ( WtF wins as Death Rage has real consequance, have in-character support by Triggers mechanics, and is known horrors films 'I killed my family, now you all join me or die trying to stop me' )</li> <li>Horror of the ultimate hopelessness of you action - Horror of losing your sense of yourself - becoming 'mindless beast' OR clueless human, both ending with 'monsterous' werewolf life.</li> </ul>Beside those, points that come in favor of WtF:<ul><li><b>Tribes - </b>They are PCs splats to choose in both games. In WtA Tribes are ethnic stereotypes that are, let's just say, a bit offensive to minorities, sometimes. In WtF Tribes are more like churches of particular Great Wolf Hunter ( Firstborn ) and hunting school for particular Sacred Prey ( see below ). It looks a bit artificial here, but I asses you, it's much more visecral than WtA groups.</li> <li><b>Humans are REAL threat</b> - but not because they lay trash everywhere - there is one WtF Tribe that says Humans are most dangerous Prey as they are most numerous. They hunt for gangs, corrupted police, sects or organized crime - all in the light that if those forces would all uncover existence of werewolves - the whole race would be screwed if humanity join forces. They also like to track other supernatural beings.</li> <li><b>Sacred Hunt</b> - WtF werewolves are slave to inner need of Hunt. They NEED to chase after they Prey, no matter what it is. It's maybe less romantic story than WtA 'We must defend Mother Earth', but it's clearly more horror like. You are Ultimate Predator and you need to Hunt - even if this will cost you your life. Because it most surely it will, someday.</li> <li><b>Toolbox</b> - For some it's probably the problem, but to me it's greatest asset of the WtF. There is very little of hard canon. All of the things I pointed are in there, but games do not force you to explore most of it if you do not want. All that is needed is story and if you have many Tribes in group it's good - but not needed - to have all major 5 antagonists groups. You can add or take as much as you like - game is DESIGNED to be easily changed and not follow one and only true narrative.</li> </ul>Once again, like with all WoD vs CoD comparison - WoD is better story on paper, CoD is much better RPG game on same tropes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-03-2018, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:34:39-07:00","id":1214893,"title":"","content":"Speaking of tribes <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, how easy would it be to make a bone gnawer inspired clan of iron masters. I'm asking because bone gnawers were by far my favorite for being a literal underdog and being so dignified about it, ESPECIALLY in their creed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:37:51-07:00","id":1214894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1214387-since-i-don-t-know-where-to-put-this?p=1214802#post1214802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they make up the external horror perfectly. And how does forsaken handle the internal horror</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to mark that for me, WtF make External Horror as good as WtA, as I pointed elements above. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To sum up the most important points about Internal Horror in WtF:<ul><li><b>Harmony</b> - If you become to much Flesh ( human-like ) or Spirit ( 'spiritual wolf-like ) you end as 'clueless human that kills his village every one month' or 'always changing forms mostrocity that follows alien Bans', respecitvely. So thread carefully and balance your actions</li> <li><b>Death Rage</b> - Each werewolf have Triggers that starts his Rage. Beside typical like 'they are killing my family' or 'I'm almost dying' each wolf has his own Triggers. Most often is 'Moon in the particular phase', 'I sense blood' or 'there is monster in here', but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers\">one devs made great extra list</a> like 'I hate being betrayed', 'you must listen all to me', 'I did not eat a day or two' or even 'he offended me'. You create those lists of what is most irritating to character - and then watch how he become killing machine on those events. More Harmony is on extremes, it's much easier for character on most trivial things to go on Rage.</li> <li><b>Touchstones </b>- To not go out of balance Harmony quickly, werewolves develop Touchstones, close relations that grips him in one side of Flesh-Spirit balance. Most often they are his lovers, family, friends or even favorite place on Flesh side - and wolf spirit, private place in spirit world or just strange, living item on another. You want to really fuck some werewolf - destroy his Touchstones. And see how he will kill his pack in Death Rage then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-03-2018, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:42:03-07:00","id":1214895,"title":"","content":"SubTribes - or rather Hunting Cults - in <b>WtF</b> are called Lodges. I <i>literally</i> have my private project of remaking <b>WtA</b> Tribes as Lodges in <b>WtF 2E</b> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1081045-wyrd-s-lodges-hub\">here is main topic</a>. And here are <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1205625-2e-wta-tribe-as-wtf-lodge-%E2%80%93-bone-gnawers\">Bone Gnawers</a> </b>as mostly Iron Masters and Bone Shadows Lodge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:43:48-07:00","id":1214896,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much wyrdhamster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}